      "title": "Spanish transport minister resigns after deadly train crash",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/03/spain-transport-minister-oscar-puente-resigns-deadly-train-crash",
      "description": "<p>Óscar Puente also announces his withdrawal from upcoming election following disaster that killed 69 people</p><p>Spain’s transport minister handed in his resignation on Tuesday after the train crash that <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/02/spain-train-crash-us-citizens-japan-canada-dead\">killed 69 people</a> last week, one of the worst railway disasters in Europe this century.</p><p>Óscar Puente, who had earlier pledged to work “tirelessly” to restore confidence in the world’s second-largest high-speed rail network, also said he was withdrawing from the country’s upcoming general election.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/03/spain-transport-minister-oscar-puente-resigns-deadly-train-crash\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
